---
/* About › Overview — what MOSAIC is and who it serves. */
import ContentCard from '../ui/ContentCard.astro'

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL
---

<div class="ov-split">
  <div class="ov-text">
    <p>
      MOSAIC is a catalogue and set of connectors that show what geospatial data exists for living
      landscapes, who produced it, at what resolution and time period, and how to access it. Its
      guiding principle is to connect, not duplicate: it links the global data services the world
      already maintains with the local datasets only CGIAR holds.
    </p>
    <p>
      Data files stay with the institution that produced them and are linked from each catalogue
      entry. Every entry carries a readiness status, from first registration through to
      analytics-ready.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="ov-art" aria-hidden="true">
    <img src={`${base}/illustrations/network-diagram.png`} alt="" />
  </div>
</div>

<h3 class="ov-h3">Who it serves</h3>
<p class="ov-lead">Anyone working with data for living landscapes — research institutions, universities, public agencies, NGOs, landscape initiatives and independent researchers.</p>
<div class="ov-cards">
  <ContentCard icon="users" title="Data users" tint="teal">
    Researchers, GIS analysts, decision-makers and landscape teams who need to know what data
    exists for a landscape and how to get it.
  </ContentCard>
  <ContentCard icon="upload" title="Data contributors" tint="amber">
    Data stewards and focal points who want their datasets to be findable, documented and
    reusable. <a href="#contribute">How to contribute &rarr;</a>
  </ContentCard>
</div>

<style>
  .ov-split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr; gap: var(--space-8); align-items: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-12); }
  .ov-text p { color: var(--color-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); }
  .ov-text p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .ov-art img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .ov-h3 { font-size: var(--text-2xl); margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); }
  .ov-lead { color: var(--color-muted); margin: 0 0 var(--space-6); max-width: 62ch; line-height: 1.6; }
  .ov-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-6); }
  .ov-cards a { color: var(--mosaic-teal); font-weight: 600; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .ov-cards a { color: var(--mosaic-light-teal); }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .ov-split, .ov-cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
